Here's the heart of the matter then.  Exponent is the name of the Newsletter
published by ExI, the Extropy Institute for members of that august body.
No different than Extropy, Exponent is therefor reserved as a distincitve
name for a publication, whether print or electronic.   

As to whether ExI should take action, I really don't see it as being in their
interest.  And as Tom Morrow has pointed out, there is necessarily a degree
of uncertainty as to whether it is an actionable claim.  Nontheless, the
notion that one can trademark words with mundane meenings is well established,
and the existence of Exponent, the ExI newsletter should therefor dispell
any reservations you have about whether ExI can hold a trademark in that 
name.



